    <description>LFRDN-606: routes a new Lead to the correct shared CRM queue by Brand, so a CRM Agent/Manager can self-assign from it - replaces AF_FL_Lead_RoundRobinAssignment (deactivated) now that AF_VR_Lead_OwnerAssignByManagerOnly blocks self-service reassignment away from a Manager/Supervisor. Built directly against AF_Brand__c (present at insert time) rather than the Assignment Rule (AF_AR_Lead_Routing), because Database.DMLOptions().assignmentRuleHeader was confirmed unreliable on Lead INSERT in this org (works fine on a subsequent UPDATE, tested directly) - the Assignment Rule is left in place for manual &quot;reassign&quot; use in Setup but is no longer relied on for the create-time routing decision. Mirrors the same Brand-to-queue mapping as the Assignment Rule: Ferrari -&gt; SportsMotors, Rolls-Royce -&gt; Automobiles, everything else -&gt; Review (full brand list still TBP).

BRD 8.4 FR5 (queue-addition notification): after routing, looks up the queue&apos;s direct User members and sends them a single Custom Notification. The loop only builds the recipient collection (Assignment only, no action call inside it) — Send_Notification fires once, after the loop, with the whole collection, not once per member. Pairs with AF_FL_Lead_NotifyOnAssignment, which fires the second FR5 notification when a Manager hands the Lead off to an individual agent.</description>
    <environments>Default</environments>
    <formulas>
        <name>Coalesce_Queue_Id</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>IF(NOT(ISBLANK({!Get_SportsMotors_Queue.Id})), {!Get_SportsMotors_Queue.Id}, IF(NOT(ISBLANK({!Get_Automobiles_Queue.Id})), {!Get_Automobiles_Queue.Id}, {!Get_Review_Queue.Id}))</expression>
    </formulas>
    <interviewLabel>Lead Queue Routing {!$Flow.CurrentDateTime}</interviewLabel>
